    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is ClickUp better than monday.com?</h3>
    <p>ClickUp is better for teams that want maximum customization and a single tool to replace multiple apps. It offers more views, more features, and deeper free-tier functionality than monday.com. monday.com is better for teams that want a simpler, more visual tool that is easy to adopt. ClickUp has a steeper learning curve but more power. monday.com is more polished and faster to roll out. For complex workflows, choose ClickUp. For simplicity and speed, choose monday.com.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, ClickUp or monday.com?</h3>
    <p>ClickUp is cheaper. ClickUp Unlimited costs $7 per user per month, while monday.com Standard costs $9 per user per month. ClickUp also offers a stronger free plan with unlimited tasks and users, while monday.com limits the free plan to 2 users. At scale, ClickUp Business costs $12 per user versus monday.com Pro at $19 per user. For budget-conscious teams, ClickUp offers more features per dollar.</p>

    <h3>Which has better automation, ClickUp or monday.com?</h3>
    <p>monday.com has better automation for most users. Its automation builder is visual, intuitive, and requires no technical knowledge. You can create rules like when status changes to Done, notify the team. ClickUp automations are powerful but require more configuration and have a steeper learning curve. For non-technical teams that want to automate workflows quickly, monday.com wins. For teams that need complex conditional automations, ClickUp offers more depth.</p>

    <h3>Can I migrate from monday.com to ClickUp?</h3>
    <p>Yes, you can migrate from monday.com to ClickUp. ClickUp offers a built-in import tool that pulls tasks, statuses, and assignees from monday.com. The process is automated but may require manual cleanup for custom fields and complex dependencies. Most teams complete a migration in 1 to 3 days depending on workspace size. ClickUp also offers white-glove migration assistance on Business plans and above.</p>

    <h3>Which is better for Agile teams, ClickUp or monday.com?</h3>
    <p>ClickUp is better for Agile teams. It includes native sprint management, story points, burndown charts, and Agile dashboards on all paid plans. monday.com offers Agile features through its monday dev product, which is sold separately and adds cost. For Scrum or Kanban teams that want built-in Agile tooling without paying extra, ClickUp is the stronger choice. For teams that prefer a simpler board-only workflow, monday.com works well.</p>

    <h3>Can I use ClickUp and monday.com together?</h3>
    <p>It is not practical to use both platforms for the same team, but some organizations use ClickUp for engineering and monday.com for marketing or operations. This creates silos and requires integrations to sync data. Most teams pick one platform and standardize. If you have departments with very different workflows, using both may make sense, but the overhead of maintaining two systems usually outweighs the benefits.</p>

